"siri_help" = "On iPhone, Siri and Shortcuts can tune channels by name or number, read what’s on now and next, search the guide, open a channel guide, and pause, resume or stop playback. Include the app name in your request. Siri asks for the search text. Add a playlist and open the app once to import its guide. Answers use the imported guide. These actions also work without Apple Intelligence; onscreen channel context needs iOS 18.2 or later and system support. For example, say “Watch BBC One in Accessible IPTV”; “IPTV” also works as the app name. Siri knows favourites, recent channels and the first 100 in the playlist by name; on iOS 18 and later, Spotlight finds them too. If Shortcuts lists no actions, open the app once after installing or updating.";
